WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.076 --> 00:00:20.100
August 25 Dear Daddy Longlegs, Well, Jervie is here, and we're having such a nice time!

2
00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.622
At least I am, and I hope he is too.

3
00:00:24.962 --> 00:00:28.424
He has been here ten days and doesn't show any signs of leaving.

4
00:00:30.336 --> 00:00:30.956
The way Mrs.

5
00:00:31.016 --> 00:00:32.997
Semple spoils him is awful!

6
00:00:34.377 --> 00:00:37.318
I don't understand how he turned out to be such a nice person.

7
00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:43.760
He and I eat at a little table set on the side porch, or sometimes under the trees.

8
00:00:46.021 --> 00:00:49.702
He just picks the spot where he wants to eat, and the maid brings out the table and

9
00:00:49.742 --> 00:00:57.004
dishes. If she has to carry the food very far, he leaves her a dollar under the sugar

10
00:00:57.044 --> 00:01:00.673
bowl. Jervie doesn't seem like a Pendleton at all.

11
00:01:01.673 --> 00:01:03.534
He's so simple and sweet.

12
00:01:05.235 --> 00:01:08.476
I know that seems like a funny way to describe a man, but it's true.

13
00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:13.758
Unlike Julia, he doesn't care if people belong to the right sort of family.

14
00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:17.620
He's extremely nice to the farmers around here.

15
00:01:18.961 --> 00:01:22.442
They were suspicious of him at first, but now they like to talk to him.

16
00:01:24.703 --> 00:01:26.724
It seems they didn't like his clothes very much!

17
00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:30.746
I must say, his clothes are rather amazing.

18
00:01:31.806 --> 00:01:33.827
He often wears white flannel trousers.

19
00:01:34.988 --> 00:01:36.409
Just like a proper gentleman!

20
00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:42.172
The other day we were going riding, and he came downstairs in fancy riding pants.

21
00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:44.734
"Oh my!"

22
00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:50.017
Mrs. Semple walked around him and admired his clothes from every angle.

23
00:01:50.037 --> 00:01:52.518
"Be careful where you sit.

24
00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:55.420
You don't want to get those new clothes dirty."

25
00:01:56.848 --> 00:01:57.988
Jervie rolled his eyes.

26
00:01:58.008 --> 00:02:01.029
"Run along and do your work, Mrs.

27
00:02:01.089 --> 00:02:04.290
Semple. You can't tell me what to do anymore.

28
00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:05.470
I've grown up."

29
00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:11.192
"Why, Jervie Pendleton, you can't talk to me like that!"

30
00:02:12.772 --> 00:02:16.293
Mrs. Semple pretended to be annoyed, but I could tell she was proud of him.

31
00:02:16.313 --> 00:02:24.055
"I remember when I used to wash your face while you sat on my lap."

32
00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:25.256
I burst out laughing.

33
00:02:27.988 --> 00:02:29.229
I couldn't help myself!

34
00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.270
"Why are you laughing?"

35
00:02:32.671 --> 00:02:33.691
they both said at once.

36
00:02:33.711 --> 00:02:38.814
"He's so tall that it's hard to imagine him sitting on your lap!"

37
00:02:39.174 --> 00:02:39.735
I replied.

38
00:02:40.935 --> 00:02:42.896
And he is tall, Daddy Longlegs.

39
00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.298
Almost as tall as you.

40
00:02:45.318 --> 00:02:48.679
"Well, he did," Mrs.

41
00:02:48.739 --> 00:02:49.340
Semple said.

42
00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.801
"And you should have seen Mrs.

43
00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.702
Semple back then," Jervie said.

44
00:02:53.722 --> 00:02:56.764
"She could run faster than I could!"

45
00:02:58.012 --> 00:03:00.513
"So if he escaped from my lap, I could catch him!

46
00:03:02.073 --> 00:03:04.434
Now run along, you two, I have work to do."

47
00:03:06.374 --> 00:03:08.435
We've been having so many adventures.

48
00:03:12.536 --> 00:03:16.997
We've explored the country for miles, and Jervie has even taught me how to fish.

49
00:03:19.738 --> 00:03:24.679
August 28 We climbed Sky Hill yesterday afternoon.

50
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:26.900
That's a mountain near the farm.

51
00:03:28.588 --> 00:03:29.748
There's no snow on the top.

52
00:03:31.469 --> 00:03:35.150
It's not that high, but you're still pretty breathless when you reach the top.

53
00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:38.211
"Let's stay and watch the sunset," Jervie said.

54
00:03:38.231 --> 00:03:41.072
"We'll build a fire and cook our supper."

55
00:03:41.092 --> 00:03:45.253
"I'd like to see the sun go down," I said.

56
00:03:45.273 --> 00:03:49.514
"But I've never cooked outside before, never mind built a fire."

57
00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.475
"Don't worry about a thing.

58
00:03:53.535 --> 00:03:54.176
I'll do the cooking.

59
00:03:54.556 --> 00:03:55.256
I'm used to camping."

60
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.721
So we had a delicious supper and watched the sunset.

61
00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:05.924
We came back down the mountain by moonlight.

62
00:04:07.344 --> 00:04:11.266
Fortunately, Jervie had a lantern, so we could find our way down the trail.

63
00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:14.808
It was so much fun!

64
00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:19.950
He laughed and joked and talked about such interesting things.

65
00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.612
He has read all the books I've read, plus so many more.

66
00:04:26.836 --> 00:04:29.217
It's amazing how many different things he knows.

67
00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:35.520
September 3 I still haven't finished this letter!

68
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.561
Let me tell you what happened on Sunday morning.

69
00:04:38.581 --> 00:04:44.143
"We must leave here by ten to get to church on time," Mrs.

70
00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.204
Semple said to Jervie.

71
00:04:45.224 --> 00:04:47.625
"Very well, Mrs.

72
00:04:47.685 --> 00:04:50.186
Semple, you get the buggy ready," he replied.

73
00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:53.307
"But if I'm not dressed, go without me."

74
00:04:54.747 --> 00:04:57.145
"Oh, we'll wait," she said firmly.

75
00:04:57.165 --> 00:04:59.966
"As you wish," he said.

76
00:04:59.986 --> 00:05:02.888
"But don't keep the horses standing too long."

77
00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:08.611
Then when she was dressing for church, he told me to change into my regular clothes.

78
00:05:10.092 --> 00:05:12.153
We slipped out the back door and went fishing!

79
00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:16.516
Did you ever hear anything so funny?

80
00:05:18.016 --> 00:05:20.398
We cooked our fish over a campfire for lunch.

81
00:05:22.619 --> 00:05:26.289
We didn't get home until four and then we went driving at five.

82
00:05:28.489 --> 00:05:31.110
Mrs. Semple was disappointed that we didn't go to church.

83
00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.371
She blamed herself for not training Jervie better when he was young.

84
00:05:37.912 --> 00:05:42.473
But we think she was upset about something else—she wanted to show him off to her friends at

85
00:05:42.513 --> 00:05:51.175
church! September 8 I'm sure you must move in the same social circles as Jervis Pendleton.

86
00:05:51.975 --> 00:05:53.536
I wanted to ask him if he knew you.

87
00:05:54.976 --> 00:05:58.160
But I couldn't because I don't know your real name.

88
00:06:00.002 --> 00:06:00.623
You're Mr.

89
00:06:00.743 --> 00:06:01.344
Smith to me.

90
00:06:01.765 --> 00:06:02.846
Isn't that silly?

91
00:06:02.866 --> 00:06:08.493
I've been writing this letter for two weeks, so it's time I finally mailed it!

92
00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:12.598
Affectionately, Judy
